This sidecar exists because JSON has no comment syntax and Claude Code's settings loader
warns on unrecognised top-level keys — a behaviour that could not be verified against a
running Claude Code from the build machine, so no commentary key was risked inside the
file itself. The rationale for every entry in `permissions.allow` and `permissions.deny`
is in `runbooks/steward-operations.md`, section "The allowlist is the capability
boundary", and `tests/integration/steward/test_capability_boundary.py` asserts the two
agree.
